[I] A small utility to wait for network peer availability

[T] wait4ports polls a list of addresses and TCP ports, sleeping between
[T] rounds, until all of them accept connections. It is designed for
[T] docker-compose style containers that need to wait for linked services to
[T] be ready, and supports hostname lookups, IPv6 and named services.

[U] https://github.com/erikogan/wait4ports

[A] Wait4ports Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

